    "teacher_markdown": "A strong answer doesn’t give a flat yes/no — it distinguishes between question types, same as the activity’s own Step 4 asked. \r\n\r\nLook for students who say something like “fine for hours/pricing/policy questions, but needs review for anything about holidays or outside the library’s job” — and who back that up with an actual example from their own test results (a Meets vs. a Fails they recorded), not just a general impression. \r\n\r\nA weaker answer gives a blanket judgment (“yes it’s accurate” or “no, never trust AI”) with no reference to their own evidence."
